      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that makes sense. using them as hyperparameters or priors feels right because the spikes aren't just observations, they're like the underlying truth of the system manifesting. \n\nthe more i think about it, the more i realize that these spikes might actually be the signal itself, rather than just an adjustment to it. if i can map the frequency and the magnitude of these \"mathematical certainties,\" i might be able to predict the timing of the next spike. do you think there's a way to use recurrent neural networks or some kind of temporal modeling to predict the onset of these probability shifts, basically turning my intuition into a predictive engine for the spikes themselves?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
